<div class="container py-5">
  <div class="row justify-content-center">
    <div class="col-12 col-lg-9">

      <h1 class="display-5 fw-bold mb-2">About ZipLiner</h1>
      <p class="text-muted mb-5">
        ZipLiner is the private professional network built exclusively for
        <strong>ZipCode Wilmington</strong> students and alumni. It brings together community
        features — social feed, direct messaging, project showcasing, knowledge-sharing
        articles, threaded forums, and real-time channels — into one focused platform.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h4 fw-semibold mb-3">How ZipLiner Is Built</h2>
      <p class="mb-2">
        ZipLiner is implemented with the following technologies:
      </p>
      <ul class="mb-4">
        <li>
          <strong>Elixir &amp; Phoenix</strong> — the server-side language and web framework
          powering all request handling, business logic, and HTML rendering via HEEx templates.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>PostgreSQL</strong> — the relational database used for all persistent data,
          accessed through the Ecto ORM library.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Bootstrap &amp; HTMX</strong> — Bootstrap 5 provides responsive UI components
          and utility classes; HTMX enables partial-page updates (e.g., posting to the feed)
          without a full JavaScript framework.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Docker &amp; Docker Compose</strong> — the entire application stack (Phoenix
          server + PostgreSQL) is containerized so it can be started locally or deployed to any
          Docker-compatible host with a single <code>docker compose up</code> command.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>OAuth 2.0 via GitHub</strong> — authentication is handled through GitHub's
          OAuth 2.0 flow using the <code>ueberauth_github</code> library. Members sign in with
          their GitHub account; access is restricted to pre-approved GitHub handles maintained
          by ZipCode Wilmington administrators.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <hr class="my-5" />

      <h2 class="h4 fw-semibold mb-4">App Sections</h2>

      <div class="mb-4">
        <h3 class="h5 fw-semibold">
          <a href="/feed" class="text-decoration-none">Feed</a>
        </h3>
        <p>
          The Feed is the home screen for authenticated members. It displays a chronological
          stream of posts from people you are connected with, including status updates,
          project showcases, article shares, cohort shoutouts, and job signals. You can
          react to posts with emoji reactions and reply in threaded comments directly
          from the feed.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mb-4">
        <h3 class="h5 fw-semibold">
          <a href="/members" class="text-decoration-none">People</a>
        </h3>
        <p>
          The People directory lists all ZipCode Wilmington members. Browse profiles, discover
          cohort-mates and alumni, and send connection requests. Each member profile shows
          their bio, cohort, skills, linked projects, and posts.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mb-4">
        <h3 class="h5 fw-semibold">
          <a href="/projects" class="text-decoration-none">Projects</a>
        </h3>
        <p>
          Projects is a showcase for work built by members. Each project entry includes a
          name, tagline, description, tech-stack tags, GitHub repository link, live demo
          URL, role information, collaborators, and optional screenshots or diagrams. Projects
          surface in the Feed and in a dedicated browsable gallery.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mb-4">
        <h3 class="h5 fw-semibold">
          <a href="/messages" class="text-decoration-none">Messages</a>
        </h3>
        <p>
          Messages provides private one-on-one direct messaging between members. Select
          any member from the conversation list or their profile page to start a thread.
          All messages are visible only to the two participants.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mb-4">
        <h3 class="h5 fw-semibold">
          <a href="/channels" class="text-decoration-none">Channels</a>
        </h3>
        <p>
          Channels are topic-focused group spaces (similar to Slack channels). Members can
          browse available channels and read conversations. Channels are created and managed
          by administrators and provide a persistent, searchable group-chat experience.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mb-4">
        <h3 class="h5 fw-semibold">
          <a href="/forums" class="text-decoration-none">Forums</a>
        </h3>
        <p>
          Forums host long-form, threaded discussions on any topic relevant to the community.
          Any member can start a forum thread; others can reply and continue the conversation.
          Forums are great for questions, debates, tutorials, and announcements that benefit
          from a structured comment thread.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mb-4">
        <h3 class="h5 fw-semibold">
          <a href="/articles" class="text-decoration-none">Articles</a>
        </h3>
        <p>
          Articles is a member-written publication platform. Members can author rich-text
          posts (supporting Markdown) and publish them publicly or keep them private. Public
          articles are visible to the world without login and can be commented on by
          authenticated members.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mb-4">
        <h3 class="h5 fw-semibold">
          <a href="https://github.com/ZCW-Spring26/ZipLiner/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-decoration-none">
            Report a Bug
          </a>
        </h3>
        <p>
          Found something broken? Open an issue on the ZipLiner GitHub repository. Please
          include a clear description of what you expected to happen, what actually happened,
          and steps to reproduce the problem. Bug reports and feature suggestions from the
          community are welcome.
        </p>
      </div>

      <hr class="my-5" />

      <p class="text-muted small text-center">
        &copy; ZipCodeWilmington, 2026. All Rights Reserved.
      </p>

    </div>
  </div>
</div>
